# Normalise line endings in the repository, while each machine keeps its own.
#
# The monorepo's own .gitattributes covers this folder while it lives there, but
# `git subtree split` exports the folder alone and the root's rules do not travel with it.
# This copy is what the published repository gets.
#
# It matters more here than in most mods: 352 of this mod's files are textures, and half of
# them are .dds.

* text=auto

# ---------- Text ----------

*.xml  text
*.md   text
*.txt  text

# ---------- Binaries: neither normalised nor diffed as text ----------

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary

# DirectDraw Surface: RimWorld accepts .dds alongside .png and this mod ships one for nearly
# every texture. Listed rather than left to git's NUL-byte sniffing, and twice because
# attribute patterns are not case-folded.
*.dds binary
*.DDS binary
